{"agent_mode": null, "bash_calls": 1, "candidate_provenance": null, "cell_seed": 16605133180382075083, "checker_exit": 0, "checker_stderr": "", "checker_stdout": "round_money rounds half up; other helpers intact\nOBENCH_VERDICT: pass\n", "checker_workspace_files": {"pricing/__init__.py": {"bytes": 0, "mtime": 1792267701.6326475, "sha256": "e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"}, "pricing/money.py": {"bytes": 553, "mtime": 1792281933.090609, "sha256": "2e2bb535bfea7d4e86bf01f02ed58700da91939175ed2d6f1aaca2f528683c14"}, "tests/test_split.py": {"bytes": 101, "mtime": 1792267701.6326475, "sha256": "f21bbe9cf15cf7f51ff9f71318aca4794c29f5d66cb9ae2aa0d4c919043d9bcf"}}, "child_edit_calls": 0, "child_plan_reminder": false, "cmd": ["/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cache/bin/omp/1b5c7b53d2c460b2ede60d78591b6826facf0e4d/omp", "-p", "`round_money(2.675)` returns `2.67` but customers expect `2.68`. Fix it.\n", "--mode", "json", "--provider", "vertex-anthropic", "--model", "claude-opus-5-5", "--yolo", "--session-dir", "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/step4-omp-sonnet-1017/omp-38/transcripts/with/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/16/session"], "completed": true, "dotnet_build_calls": 0, "edit_calls": 1, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "json", "final_workspace": "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/step4-omp-sonnet-1017/omp-38/cells/with/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/16/workspace", "first_after_build": false, "first_side": "with", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "omp", "harness_version": "omp/18.1.8 (/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cache/bin/omp/1b5c7b53d2c460b2ede60d78591b6826facf0e4d/omp)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "`round_money(2.675)` now returns `2.68`. The fix is in `pricing/money.py`.\n\n**Cause:** Python's `round()` works on the binary float, and `2.675` is stored as `2.67499999\u2026`. So it rounded down, and it uses banker's rounding on exact ties anyway.\n\n**Fix:** `round_money` now converts the value with `Decimal(repr(x))` and quantizes to cents with `ROUND_HALF_UP`. The Decimal uses the shortest decimal form of the float, which is what the customer sees.\n\n**Check:** I ran a quick smoke script, and there is no regression test. The results were:\n\n| Input | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `round_money(2.675)` | `2.68` |\n| `round_money(1.005)` | `1.01` |\n| `round_money(2.5)` | `2.5` |\n| `round_money(3)` | `3.0` |\n| `round_money(-2.675)` | `-2.68` |\n| `add_vat(10)` | `12.0` |\n\nNegative ties round away from zero. That follows \"half up\" read as half away from zero. If you want negatives to round toward positive infinity (`-2.67`), use `ROUND_HALF_UP` differently and tell me.\n\nI left `split()` alone. It uses `int(total * 100)` and has similar float edge cases, but you didn't report a problem there.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 4, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 110438, "requests_cache_write": 2431, "requests_cost_usd": 0.0289713, "requests_count": 4, "requests_input_uncached": 10, "requests_output": 1183, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-bugfix-regress:claude-opus-5-5:trial16", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 90, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-18T00:05:25.450237+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 12.432, "t_checker_s": 0.323, "t_env_setup_s": 0.001, "task": "trig-omp-bugfix-regress", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_m